# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every tracked text file is stored in Git with LF line endings, but
# `.gitattributes` was absent until v1.0.1, so that was an accident of history
# rather than a stated policy. `* text=auto` states it.
#
# This adds no renormalisation commit: all 27 text blobs are already LF, so
# nothing is rewritten. It only stops a future contributor whose
# `core.autocrlf` is false from committing CRLF blobs that would silently
# diverge from the ones already in the repository.
#
# What it deliberately does *not* do is pin the working-tree line ending. Git
# still checks out with the platform's native ending (CRLF on Windows, LF
# elsewhere). That is harmless here, because the artifacts under `results/`
# are written with pandas `to_csv` and `json.dump`, both of which also use the
# platform's native newline, so a regenerated artifact still matches the
# checked-out one byte for byte on either platform. The reproduction record in
# REPRODUCTION.md depends on exactly that property.
* text=auto
